===Etymology===
There are several theories. The word may derived from an {{etyl|it}} slang term {{term|fugazi||fake|lang=it}}; it may be a slang version of ''fugacious'', from {{etyl|la}} ''fugac-'', the stem of {{term|fugax|fugāx|ready to flee, flying|lang=la}}, hence "fleeting, transitory". Alternatively, it may relate to the Italian term {{term|fougasse||land mine|lang=it}}.

Folk etymology considers the military sense an abbreviation of "fucked up, got ambushed, zipped in" (a body bag).

